       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the 4,000 mg/day ceiling. It carries a serious risk of acute liver injury, and I don't know of any clinical scenario that justifies it. You also didn't give a rationale, such as a specific protocol, so I can't treat this as a deliberate exception.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 8 hours (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4 g/day, the maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 4-6 hours, capped at 4 g/day\n\nIf the pain is not controlled on these, I can enter a multimodal regimen, for example with an NSAID or another adjunct, if you tell me which one. If you still want the 2000 mg three-times-daily dose, please talk to pharmacy first. It would need to go through their review and your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nWhich regimen would you like me to enter?"
      }
